Aldgate
[vignette intro/city_gates]

FIXME(mundane): PC arrives at Aldgate at the end of a weeks-long caravan crossing — cold nights, thin meals, pack beasts, old leather. The caravan is halted outside the gate among weathered crates, trade cloth, and dusty barrels. Mules in their traces; imperial banners above the gate.
FIXME(mundane): The caravan master is caught in a growing dispute with imperial functionaries at the gate. He looks to the PC for help.
FIXME(mundane): PC declines — they will have trouble enough in the city; lets the master handle his own affairs. The caravan idles in the road. Nothing moves but the wind and the mules.
FIXME(dread): PC notices an unfamiliar weight on their hand
